'''''Goeppertia concinna''''' (syn. ''Calathea concinna'', ''Calathea leopardina'') is a species of flowering plant from the genus ''[[Goeppertia]]'' in the family [[Marantaceae]].<ref name="RHS_357162">{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/357162/goeppertia-concinna/details |title=Houseplants Conservatory Greenhouse ''Goeppertia concinna'' elegant calathea |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2026 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=7 June 2026 |quote=RHS Plants Shop Buy online from £17.99 ... 3 suppliers }}</ref> It is native to Espírito Santo and Minas Gerais in southeastern Brazil.<ref name="POWO_60459267-2">{{cite POWO |id=60459267-2 |title=''Goeppertia concinna'' (W.Bull) Borchs. & S.Suárez |access-date=7 June 2026 }}</ref> A perennial shrub of the wet tropics, it has found use as a houseplant.<ref name="RHS_357162" /> 

== Description ==
[[File:Goeppertia concinna inflorescence.jpg|left|thumb|180x180px|Inflorescence of ''Goeppertia concinna'']]

''Goeppertia concinna'' is a small sized plant. It has pointy, light green [[Leaf|leaves]], long, green [[Petiole (botany)|petioles]] and a small, green [[pulvinus]]. It has a pattern on the upper side of the leaf, which consists of a few, pointy dark green spots along the middle vein. The [[inflorescence]] of ''G.concinna'' is made of multiple [[Bract|bracts]] on a very short [[Peduncle (botany)|peduncle]]. The bracts are pointy and green and the [[Flower|flowers]] are bright yellow.<ref>{{Cite book |last1=Eichler |first1=August Wilhelm |url=http://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/bibliography/454 |title=Flora Brasiliensis, enumeratio plantarum in Brasilia hactenus detectarum: quas suis aliorumque botanicorum studiis descriptas et methodo naturali digestas partim icone illustratas /ediderunt Carolus Fridericus Philippus de Martius et Augustus Guilielmus Eichler; iisque defunctis successor Ignatius Urban. |last2=Endlicher |first2=István László |last3=Fenzl |first3=Eduard |last4=Martius |first4=Karl Friedrich Philipp von |last5=Mary |first5=Benj. |last6=Oldenburg |first6=R. |last7=Urban |first7=Ignaz |date=1840 |publisher=R. Oldenbourg |location=Monachii et Lipsiae [Munich & Leipzig] |doi=10.5962/bhl.title.454 }}</ref>

== Taxonomy ==
In 2012, Mariana Saka, stated that the old type of ''Calathea leopardina'' was now used for ''Goeppertia concinna'' as [[Eduard August von Regel|Regel]] considered ''Calathea leopardina'' only a variety of ''Calathea concinna'' (''Calathea leopardina var.''concinna). The only differentiation Regel noticed between the two was the shape of the leaves (elliptic vs elliptic lanceolate).<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Saka |first1=Mariana Naomi |last2=Lombardi |first2=Julio Antonio |date=2015-08-14 |title=Nomenclatural notes on ''Goeppertia'' (Marantaceae) |url=https://phytotaxa.mapress.com/pt/article/view/phytotaxa.222.2.9 |journal=Phytotaxa |language=en |volume=222 |issue=2 |pages=155–158 |doi=10.11646/phytotaxa.222.2.9 |bibcode=2015Phytx.222..155S |issn=1179-3163 }}</ref>

== Cultivation ==
In cultivation, there is a species that is often misnamed as ''Goeppertia concinna'', which is a ''Goeppertia'' species called in the trade "Freddie". Those plants are a different species as ''Goeppertia concinna''. The real ''G. concinna'' is more often sold as ''Goeppertia leopardina'' (or ''Calathea leopardina''). 

